Day 31 – Number of Enclaves
Problem Solved
Number of Enclaves (LeetCode 1020)
Concepts Used
BFS / DFS
Grid Traversal
Boundary Traversal
Connected Components
Graph Representation of Matrix
Approach
Traverse all boundary cells.
Start BFS/DFS from every boundary land cell (1).
Mark all reachable land cells as visited.
Traverse the grid again.
Count all unvisited land cells.
Key Insight
Instead of directly finding enclaves:
Find all land cells connected to the boundary.
Remove them from consideration.
The remaining land cells are enclaves.
Complexity
Time: O(m × n)
Space: O(m × n)
Learning
This problem reinforced an important grid pattern:
Boundary Traversal + BFS/DFS
